      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "YAMBUKIAN (6) has been good in three starts back from a long spell, all in tougher company. Got within a head of Group 1 winner Fox Dan here two back before a fifth in the Casey Classic at Listed level last start. Top-shelf performer who is race fit now and perfectly placed with a big class drop. MADIGAN (4) didn't do a bad job when fourth in the St Arnaud Cup last time out. Draws a little lower and races well when third-up so could be ready to peak. THUNDERFIRE (2) came from the back row and finished third here last start, beaten 3.5 metres. That added to a handy record at this distance and he should get the favours from this nice draw. ISOLATION (3) led from this barrier and stuck on to finish second at this circuit and distance last start. Include.",
